course: dictionary
lesson: 14293
title: Notwithstanding: even so
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. You will meet them in rules, notices and official letters. Notwithstanding is one of them. It means in spite of something, or even though something is true. «The match will go ahead notwithstanding the rain.» The rain is there, but the match still happens. So notwithstanding means in spite of the rain.
explain: Look for the clue: something is true, but it does not stop the thing from happening. «The park stays open on Sundays, notwithstanding the wet weather.» Wet weather might normally close a park, but this one stays open anyway. Ask yourself: what would usually stop this? Then notice that the word says it did not.
explain: Notwithstanding can also stand on its own, at the end of a sentence, meaning however or all the same. «It was late. We went to the shop notwithstanding.» Here it means we went all the same, even though it was late. Swap in «even so» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Notwithstanding is a formal word; you will see it in rules and notices.
fact: «Notwithstanding» means in spite of, or even though something is true.
fact: «Notwithstanding the rain» means in spite of the rain.
fact: As an adverb, «notwithstanding» means however or all the same.
fact: Phrases such as «notwithstanding the fact that» mean the same as «even though» or «in spite of the fact that».
exercise: «The game went on, notwithstanding the thick fog.» What does notwithstanding mean here? | *In spite of the thick fog | Far away from the fog | Before the thick fog | Because of the thick fog
exercise: A notice says: «The library is open daily, notwithstanding public holidays.» What does this tell you? | The library is closed on public holidays | *The library opens even on public holidays | The library is only open on holidays | The library has no opening times
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «notwithstanding the fact that»? | *Even though | Instead of | Unless | Because
test: «Notwithstanding his tiredness, Sam finished the race.» What does notwithstanding mean? | *In spite of his tiredness | Without any running | Because of his tiredness | Before he was tired
test: «The food was cold. We ate it all, notwithstanding.» What does notwithstanding mean here? | Quickly | *All the same, however | Already | Not at all
exam: A sign says: «The pool is open notwithstanding the cold weather.» What does notwithstanding tell you about the cold weather? | It is the reason the pool closes | It means the pool is heated | It is the reason the pool opens | *It does not stop the pool from opening
